  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Alice has two objects:\n\n\nA cuboid with length AAA units, height BBB units, and width CCC units.\nA cube with an edge length of XXX units.\nAlice wants to know which of the two objects has a larger volume, or if their volumes are equal.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input will contain four space-separated integers AAA, BBB, CCC and XXX, the length of the cuboid, the width of the cuboid, the height of the cuboid, and the length of the edge of the cube.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint a single line containing the string:\n\n\n\n`\"Cuboid\"`, if the volume of the cuboid is greater than the volume of the cube.\n`\"Cube\"`, if the volume of the cube is greater than the volume of the cuboid.\n`\"Equal\"`, if both objects have equal volume.\n\nPrint the string without quotes.\n\nYou can print each character of the output in either uppercase or lowercase.\n\nFor example, the strings `Cube`, `CUBE`, `cube`, and `CuBe` are considered identical.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤A,B,C,X≤101 \\leq A,B,C,X \\leq 101≤A,B,C,X≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 3 10 3",
        "output": "Cuboid",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe volume of the cuboid is 1×3×10=301\\times 3\\times 10 = 301×3×10=30 cubic units.\nThe volume of the cube is 33=273^3 = 2733=27 cubic units.\nThe cuboid has larger volume."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 1 1 2",
        "output": "Cube",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe volume of the cuboid is 1×1×1=11\\times 1\\times 1 = 11×1×1=1 cubic units.\nThe volume of the cube is 23=82^3 = 823=8 cubic units.\nThe cube has larger volume."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "8 4 2 4",
        "output": "Equal",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe volume of the cuboid is 8×4×2=648\\times 4\\times 2 = 648×4×2=64 cubic units.\nThe volume of the cube is 43=644^3 = 6443=64 cubic units.\nBoth objects have the same volume."
      }
    ]
  },
